{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug final repair report (commit 35181363993cddedb0f44c238497b6e5e1b9ee2a).\n\nProblem: bare-repository fixture and restore operations failed under protected safe.bareRepository=explicit.\n\nProven root cause: commands that intentionally owned bare repositories erased repository-kind intent by invoking generic cwd=<bare> or git -C <bare> helpers. Git therefore treated them as implicit bare discovery and rejected them under explicit policy. Generic helpers also serve worktrees, so blanket conversion was unsafe.\n\nProof: on identical real repositories, strict implicit config/symbolic-ref/fetch returned 128, top-level --git-dir succeeded, default implicit controls succeeded, and worktree -C remained valid. Runtime tracing identified actual failing helper paths before test bodies. Invalid refs and nonexistent repositories continued to return 128. Archaeology preserved the three upkeep pins, --no-hardlinks, checked fail-fast behavior, and prior corruption defenses.\n\nTest: tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py was final-form RED before repair at all three reported setup paths. After the blind fix it exposed the previously masked production restore.git sibling, remained RED until that same mechanism was repaired, then passed GREEN. Reseeding the exact production defect (--git-dir back to -C) returned RED at the strict restore fetch; restoring the fix returned GREEN. It asserts real strict/default fixture outcomes and a genuine-error control, not private implementation structure.\n\nFix: introduced narrow bare-only Git helpers using top-level --git-dir at each semantically confirmed test helper call. infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py::_verify_restore now explicitly selects only its owned throwaway restore.git; ordinary repo operations retain shared run_git/-C behavior and exact ReclaimError detail. No Git safety setting changed.\n\nScope and safety: caller sweep found no caller depending on implicit bare discovery. This restores existing fixture/script behavior, adds no dependency or user-visible capability, introduces no retries/swallowing/skips/xfails, and weakens no assertion. All exact upkeep values, refs, refspecs, OID checks, cleanup, and checked error behavior remain.\n\nSiblings: construct sweep dispositioned all confirmed occurrences across 12 helper-owner test files plus the masked production restore path; deliberate safe.bareRepository=all exceptions in the external workflow and reconcile retry test remain untouched because they serve distinct contracts. Parity census is N/A: this is Git repository-kind targeting, not a multi-surface operation. No residual undispositioned fragility observed.\n\nReplication: full 12-file sibling suite passed 125/125 under isolated strict policy and 125/125 under isolated default policy. Held-out oracle passed; make lint, mypy/typecheck, complexity ratchet, diff-check, commit hooks, DCO, Change-Id, and commit-ticket verification passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787099629602597001,"uuid":"d37d7f45-1eed-4c94-8fd0-71b98fe76b06"}